  "interpretation": [
    "After standardizing each colony's informative annual growth series and removing the regional year mean, colony pairs on the same island share substantially more annual covariance than pairs on different islands.",
    "The signal survives exclusion of Litchfield and is present descriptively in both the early and late portions of the record.",
    "This supports island-scale demographic coherence but does not identify a coastline effect independent of distance or a specific mechanism.",
    "The earlier within-island spatial-insurance hypothesis is not supported; the dominant pattern is same-island synchrony rather than compensation."
